!Sample_data_processing = Raw snATAC-seq reads were processed using PISA (v1.1), aligned to the mouse mm10 genome with BWA, and further processed with bap2 to generate fragment files.
!Sample_data_processing = For stereo-seq data, transcripts from 100 × 100 DNBs were aggregated into bin50 units
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: rocessed data for snRNA-seq includes three standard sparse matrix files for each sample, packaged together into a single tar.gz archive. These include: barcodes.tsv.gz: Contains cell/nucleus barcode identifiers. features.tsv.gz: Contains gene feature annotations (IDs and names). matrix.mtx.gz: Contains the raw UMI count matrix in sparse format. Processed data for snATAC-seq includes standard output files from Cell Ranger ATAC for each sample, packaged together into a single tar.gz archive.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL28330
!Sample_contact_name = Ruolin,,Zhang
!Sample_contact_email = ruolinzhang0521@126.com
!Sample_contact_institute = Huazhong Agricultural University
!Sample_contact_address = No.1 Shizishan, Hongshan District, Wuhan City
!Sample_contact_city = Wuhan
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 430000
!Sample_contact_country = China
!Sample_instrument_model = DNBSEQ-T7
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic single cell
!Sample_library_strategy = ATAC-seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN60359071
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX33577161
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM9755nnn/GSM9755189/suppl/GSM9755189_0h-3-ATAC.fragments.tsv.gz
!Sample_series_id = GSE332910
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
^SAMPLE = GSM9755190
!Sample_title = Multiome, MCAO/R, 0h-3, RNA
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM9755190
!Sample_status = Public on Sep 09 2026
!Sample_submission_date = May 22 2026
!Sample_last_update_date = Sep 09 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = primary cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Brain
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: mixed brain cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: wild-type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: MCAO/R
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = To induce focal cerebral ischemia of mice, a silicon-coated filament was inserted into the left middle cerebral artery to block blood flow. After 60 minutes later, the filament was extracted for reperfusion.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = nuclear RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Nuclei isolation for snRNA-seq and snATAC-seq: Nuclei were isolated from frozen striatal tissues using a mechanical dissociation protocol. Briefly, frozen mouse brain were thawed on ice and homogenized in pre-chilled homogenization buffer using Dounce homogenizers. Homogenates were filtered through 40-μm cell strainers and centrifuged at 1,200 × g for 5 min at 4 °C. Nuclear pellets were resuspended in blocking buffer containing 1% BSA and 0.2 U/μL RNase inhibitor, followed by an additional centrifugation at 500 × g for 5 min. Purified nuclei were resuspended in 1% BSA for downstream library construction.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = snRNA-seq library construction and sequencing: Single-nucleus RNA-seq libraries were prepared using the DNBelab C Series High-throughput Single-Cell Library Preparation Kit. Single-nucleus suspensions were loaded onto microfluidic chips for droplet generation and incubated at room temperature for 20 min to allow mRNA capture. After emulsion breaking and bead recovery, reverse transcription and cDNA amplification were performed. DNA nanoballs were generated from purified PCR products and sequenced on the MGI DNBSEQ-Tx platform with read lengths of 41 bp (Read 1), 100 bp (Read 2), and 10 bp (index). snATAC-Seq library preparation and sequencing: For snATAC-seq library preparation, the DNBelab C Series Single-Cell ATAC Library Prep Kit was used. Library construction was performed according to the manufacturer’s instructions, including key steps: transposition, droplet formation, PCR pre-amplification, emulsion disruption, capture bead collection, DNA amplification, and final purification. Purified libraries were sequenced on the MGI DNBSEQ-T1 platform with the following parameters: Read 1 (109 bp), Read 2 (50 bp), and sample index (10 bp). The library quality was strictly controlled before sequencing. Library concentration was quantified using the Qubit ssDNA Assay Kit to ensure DNA molecule numbers and concentrations met sequencing requirements. Additionally, library fragment size distribution was analyzed using the Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer system. Stereo-seq library preparation and sequencing: Stereo-seq libraries were constructed using the STOmics Gene Expression Kit S1 according to the manufacturer’s protocol with minor modifications. Coronal brain sections (15 μm thick) were mounted onto Stereo-seq chips and fixed in methanol at −20 °C for 30 min. After nucleic acid staining and imaging, tissue sections were permeabilized at 37 °C for 12 min. cDNA was purified using AMPure XP beads. Indexed libraries were generated and sequenced on the MGI DNBSEQ-Tx platform with read lengths of 50 bp (Read 1) and 100 bp (Read 2).
!Sample_description = Library name: 0h-3-RNA
!Sample_description = 3' mRNA (DNBelab C Series scRNA library, BGI): read1 contains cell barcode and UMI; read2 contains transcript sequence
!Sample_data_processing = Single-cell RNA-seq data were processed using Seurat (v4.4.0).
!Sample_data_processing = Raw snATAC-seq reads were processed using PISA (v1.1), aligned to the mouse mm10 genome with BWA, and further processed with bap2 to generate fragment files.
!Sample_data_processing = For stereo-seq data, transcripts from 100 × 100 DNBs were aggregated into bin50 units
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: rocessed data for snRNA-seq includes three standard sparse matrix files for each sample, packaged together into a single tar.gz archive. These include: barcodes.tsv.gz: Contains cell/nucleus barcode identifiers. features.tsv.gz: Contains gene feature annotations (IDs and names). matrix.mtx.gz: Contains the raw UMI count matrix in sparse format. Processed data for snATAC-seq includes standard output files from Cell Ranger ATAC for each sample, packaged together into a single tar.gz archive.
